This is not a direct security vulnerability, but it can cause issues in tests or when importing the app elsewhere. It can also make security testing harder.

### Recommendation

Only call `listen` when the file is run directly:

```js
if (require.main === module) {
  app.listen(PORT, () => {
    console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
  });
}

module.exports = app;
```

